invariant: INV-14
file: srv.c
catches: srv_tcp_nonblocking_test
reason: a tcp-nonblocking server takes a configuration whose on_record_out is
  NULL, so srv_out.c's emit calls through a null pointer on the first
  record of the first flight. The refusal is what lets emit skip the
  test, so dropping it turns a configuration mistake into a crash.

--- old
    return cfg->buf != NULL && cfg->send != NULL && cfg->recv != NULL &&
           cfg->buf_len >= CH_MIN_RXBUF && cfg->srv.on_record_out != NULL;
--- new
    return cfg->buf != NULL && cfg->send != NULL && cfg->recv != NULL &&
           cfg->buf_len >= CH_MIN_RXBUF;
